A||N||11||ss-ls6||Kit for a Rover 3.5L v8 swap?||||5||
Z||000000||ss-ls6||01-31-2001||07:50 PM||||I am looking to drop a 1961 Oldsmobile 215 v8 into a 1981 Fiero.  The 215 is essentially a pre 1987 Rover 3.5L v8.  Do you know where I can get an engine swap kit for this operation?  The Fiero is a v6 model with an auto tranny.  The engine is all aluminum, weighing about 100 lbs less than the stock v6.  It makes 235 hp and 310 lb/ft of torque.  Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||BroCar 87||01-31-2001||08:12 PM||||First off, The fiero was only in production from 84-88 and since you have a V6 model, it couldn't be an 84 let alone an 81. You probably mistyped it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> . As far as your conversion goes, I believe there are only kits for SBC engines. <A HREF="http://www.V8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.V8archie.com</A>  supplies most of the v8 swaps that I know of. You can use any Small Block Chevy engine with his kit.<BR>You may want to check into it. I am about to go with that swap...350 baby yea!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><BR>BroCar 87||||reg||1
Z||000002||ray b||01-31-2001||08:18 PM||||B O P or buick pontiac olds bolt patern adpt. needed like old 3.8 motor v8 archie may have some . never heard of a kit. ray||||reg||1
