Z||000009||Wade87GT||02-01-2001||09:50 AM||||Slammed Fiero is correct about the Rover 3.5 being expensive and having the starter on the wrong side. I'll ad that my Triumph TR-8 has a lot of torque and the V-8 sounds it makes tempts me into putting one in my Fiero also. I've had my TR-8 since 1982 and have researched this engine extensively. You could probably get twice the power at half the price using the pushrod 3.4L. But if you really want to do this swap, ask Cliff. Over in Europe, they put this engine in just about everything. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||sparks||02-01-2001||01:36 PM||||The Al 215 didn't have the standard BOP pattern.  Mark's right.  The 198 Fireball V6 and the 215 V8 are a more rounded bolt pattern than the BOP pattern.<P>63 sounds right for the BOP pattern.<P>See my website: <A HREF="http://incolor.inetnebr.com/asparks/BuickV6/buickinfo.html" TARGET=_blank>http://incolor.inetnebr.com/asparks/BuickV6/buickinfo.html</A>  to see the bellhousing differences.<BR><P>------------------<BR><BR>Adam Sparks||||reg||1
Z||000011||lowCG||02-03-2001||01:37 PM||||I have had a '63 Buick 4bbl 215 for a long time,and even thought about putting it in my Fiero also,but I went with a 3400TDC because it was alot easier,practically bolted right in(sounds great,less filling).<BR>The 215 is still in my basement though,maybe a Lotus seven kit someday?||||reg||1
